## Exact restored Windows source and bounded adapter

Audited the restored `gpui-pre-windows-0.3.9` source, identified by Cargo.toml metadata as Zed revision `93d745668805029476e6d7fbb19652116fed51de`. No upstream-main inference was used. [Source audit, original hash and line references](input-source-audit.md).

- Native inertia is enabled. Direct Manipulation transform increments, divided by scale factor, become logical pixel deltas with Started then Moved.
- `end_gesture` emits zero-delta Ended at READY or when a new RUNNING interrupts INERTIA. There is no public RUNNING->INERTIA event; Ended can occur after inertia. No Cancelled emission appears in this handler.
- A non-consuming window-level Capture listener, installed during paint before the editor, logs public delta/units/phase/position and actual editor focus. It sees events before the normal editor Bubble consumer.

ONE bounded native diagnostic adapter vendors the exact restored Windows crate and adds logging only in `OnViewportStatusChanged`. Only `src/direct_manipulation.rs` differs from the cached crate; hash comparison verified the other files are unchanged. Original cached source is untouched; Apache license retained. [Patch](native-diagnostic.patch).

The adapter logs raw previous/current native states and marks RUNNING->INERTIA as RELEASE_CANDIDATE, RUNNING->READY as NO_INERTIA_END_CANDIDATE, READY as FINISHED_OR_RESET, and INERTIA->RUNNING as INERTIA_INTERRUPTED. It preserves existing public phases, deltas and inertia. No second recognizer, timeout-derived release or new dependency was introduced.

These labels are deliberately candidates: no-inertia lift, pause, zero-motion contact, interruption/reset and cancellation still need assessment. This is a diagnostic seam for the release gate, not a completed carousel input adapter. Append I/O adds probe overhead and cannot support app latency benchmarks.

